# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_extractor_kotlin.py" "KOTLIN GATE: PASS" "Kotlin extractor: .kt files yield def/class + calls edges (probe snippet fix)" "Kotlin extractor: .kt files produce def/class nodes and calls edges. Root cause was that _grammar_passes_probe rejected the tree-sitter-kotlin grammar because the probe snippet 'class C { fun m() {} }' causes has_error==True in tree-sitter-kotlin 1.0.x (inline single-line body is a grammar quirk); the grammar itself is sound -- the same class with a multi-line body or an explicit return-type annotation parses with has_error==False and correctly yields class_declaration + function_declaration nodes with 'name' fields. The fix changes only the probe snippet to 'class C {\n    fun m(): Unit {}\n}', which exercises the same node types and name fields. BEFORE: 52 .kt files -> 0 def/class nodes, 0 calls edges. AFTER: 52 .kt files -> 458 def/class nodes, 702 calls edges (measured on kotlinx.coroutines/jvm/src). No dependency change (tree-sitter-kotlin>=1.0.0,<1.1 unchanged). No regex fallback needed: the grammar is sound, only the probe was wrong." "Kotlin extractor smoke: .kt fixture -> class node Repository + def nodes findById/lookup/buildRepository + at least one calls edge (calls to lookup() and Repository()); proves the probe snippet fix restored Kotlin structural extraction without a grammar or dependency change" 10
